proposed.construction:
Fix real endpoints \(L_{\mathrm{bd}}<U_{\mathrm{bd}}\) and put \(\Delta_{\mathrm{bd}}=U_{\mathrm{bd}}-L_{\mathrm{bd}}>0\).  For a bounded schedule \(\mathbf y=(y_{i1},y_{i0})_{i=1}^n\in[L_{\mathrm{bd}},U_{\mathrm{bd}}]^{2n}\), an assignment \(Z\in\{0,1\}^n\) reveals \((Z,(y_{iZ_i})_{i=1}^n)\), and its causal average treatment effect is \(n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^n(y_{i1}-y_{i0})\).  Define the balanced-complete-randomization minimax risk
\[
 \mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm{bal}}[L_{\mathrm{bd}},U_{\mathrm{bd}}]
 :=\inf_{\widehat\tau\ {
m measurable}}
 \sup_{\mathbf y\in[L_{\mathrm{bd}},U_{\mathrm{bd}}]^{2n}}
 \mathbb E_{Z\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Z_n)}
 \left[\left\{\widehat\tau\bigl(Z,(y_{iZ_i})_{i=1}^n\bigr)
 -\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^n(y_{i1}-y_{i0})\right\}^2\right].
\]
Let \(\mathfrak R_n^\star[L_{\mathrm{bd}},U_{\mathrm{bd}}]\) be the same expression with an additional outer infimum over all probability laws \(\delta\) on \(\{0,1\}^n\) and with \(Z\sim\delta\).  Thus \(\mathfrak R_n^\star\) jointly optimizes over every assignment design and every measurable estimator, whereas \(\mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm{bal}}\) fixes the balanced complete-randomization design.

